From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zeromq: include missing <condition_variable>

ZeroMQ's `condition_variable.hpp` uses `std::condition_variable_any` but
doesn't include the standard header, which causes MinGW builds to fail
with "condition_variable_any in namespace std does not name a type".
Include the header explicitly to restore Windows cross-builds.

--- a/src/condition_variable.hpp
+++ b/src/condition_variable.hpp
@@
 #include "mutex.hpp"
+#include <condition_variable>
 #include "err.hpp"
 
 namespace zmq
